/T (The US$57 gap to target is almost all the market moving from our bear case \(US$90\) to our base case \(US$148 DCF\). Three variables explain the gap: North American revenue \(base down 13.8% in the first year, bear 16% down in H1 FY27\), gross margin \(US$8 per 100bp\) and SG&A \(US$8 per 100bp\). The comparables blend adds US$7. A 12-month roll-forward would add US$16 \(US$171\) but is not applied. If Q3 and Q4 comparable sales track the bear case, the Buy should be reviewed.)
/E (The US$57 gap to target is almost all the market moving from our bear case \(US$90\) to our base case \(US$148 DCF\). Three variables explain the gap: North American revenue \(base down 13.8% in the first year, bear 16% down in H1 FY27\), gross margin \(US$8 per 100bp\) and SG&A \(US$8 per 100bp\). The comparables blend adds US$7. A 12-month roll-forward would add US$16 \(US$171\) but is not applied. If Q3 and Q4 comparable sales track the bear case, the Buy should be reviewed.)
