7442 0 obj
<<
/Title (Terminal growth of 2.5% is our judgement for a mature premium brand. We blend two terminal values equally: Gordon Growth at 2.5% and an exit multiple of 9.7x EBITDA from the comparables. The Gordon leg alone implies only 6.9x EBITDA, so the exit leg does much of the work: EV is US$16.8bn on the exit multiple and US$13.4bn on Gordon growth, a 25% gap. Terminal value is 75% of EV, so most of the value rests on 2031 and beyond. Each turn of exit multiple is worth about US$6 a share; one point off the WACC adds about US$13 and one point on takes off about US$10.)
/Dest [21 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7381 0 R
>>
endobj
